  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "How To Manage Stock Pools",
      "anchor": "how-to-manage-stock-pools"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "A Stock Pool gives business operators a reusable group of Warehouses without creating another copy of Stock. For example, an enterprise can create a `UAE_FULFILLMENT` Pool containing Dubai and Abu Dhabi Warehouses."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Before You Begin",
      "anchor": "before-you-begin"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Create the Warehouses in the same enterprise.",
        "Decide the Pool purpose and stable code.",
        "Decide membership priority. Lower numbers are considered earlier by Stock Sourcing behavior.",
        "Remember that a Pool does not make Stock available by itself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Create And Activate A Pool",
      "anchor": "create-and-activate-a-pool"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Create the Pool in `DRAFT` with its code, name, type, and optional effective dates.",
        "Add each Warehouse as a `DRAFT` membership.",
        "Set membership priority and review the ordering.",
        "Make sure the Pool and Warehouses are `ACTIVE`.",
        "Activate each membership."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The same Warehouse may participate in several Pools, but it cannot be added twice to one Pool. A membership never moves or reserves quantity."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Suspend Or Retire",
      "anchor": "suspend-or-retire"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Suspend a Pool or membership for a temporary stop. To retire a Pool, retire all of its memberships first. Never delete Pool or membership database records; retirement preserves operational history."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "What Comes Later",
      "anchor": "what-comes-later"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sourcing rules will decide when an application, country, delivery zone, channel, Store, customer segment, or item may use a Pool. Availability will then calculate eligible Stock from the member Warehouses. Neither behavior is part of the current Pool foundation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For configuration, extension, security, recovery, and test details, read the [Stock Pool foundation contract](../../gComm/inventory/docs/stock-pool-foundation.md)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Continue",
      "anchor": "continue"
    },
